// Continues inside Outer (file 2's last-closed object). Reopens Middle
// (no wrapper needed for Outer itself) and descends one level further
// into a new Leaf, so that by the time UseIt's supertype is resolved,
// this file's own {} stack is only two deep: [Middle, Leaf]. Reaching
// TOP from Leaf would need three ascends (Leaf -> Middle -> Outer -> TOP),
// so four dots (dot count N ascends N-1 levels) - the same count
// fbm-datatypes.adl uses in the real corpus this was found in, and which
// this same finding means that file now needs to stop using. This file's
// own stack can supply only one of those three levels (Leaf's own
// enclosing Middle); rather than silently continuing into the object
// tree for the other two - to Outer, opened in file 2, and to TOP,
// closed out in file 1, neither visible from here - four dots is
// rejected outright: ADLERR_ASCENT_EXCEEDS_FILE.
Middle: {
	Leaf: {
		UseIt: ....Marker;
		Proof: UseIt.Found;
	}
}
